# HTML Modernisation Skills

## Experience Summary

Modernised a legacy family-tree website archive consisting of 19 HTML pages originally generated by NetObjects Fusion 7, transforming them into cleaner, maintainable HTML5 while preserving all historical content.

## Key Skills Applied

### HTML5 Migration
- Converted HTML 4.0 Transitional documents to HTML5 (`<!DOCTYPE html>`, `<meta charset="utf-8">`)
- Removed obsolete presentational markup and generator meta tags
- Normalised tag casing while preserving uppercase conventions for minimal diff churn

### CSS Extraction & Global Styling
- Extracted repeated inline `<FONT>` styles into a single global stylesheet (`assets/css/style.css`)
- Mapped legacy font attributes to modern CSS classes:
  - `FACE="Verdana,..."` → `.font-body`
  - `FACE="Courier New Baltic,monospace"` → `.font-mono`
  - `SIZE="+2"` / `+1` / `-1` → `.font-size-large` / `.font-size-medium` / `.font-size-small`
- Preserved `<PRE>` block content exactly, only replacing wrapper `<FONT>` tags

### Asset Restructuring
- Reorganised image assets from a flat `branch/assets/images/` pool into per-branch `assets/images/` folders
- Removed spacer/clearpixel assets and empty `<td>` cells where safely possible
- Updated all relative paths across 19 HTML files to match new folder layout

### Git History Hygiene
- Squashed, reordered, and amended commits to produce a clean three-commit history
- Preserved original author identities and backdated timestamps where required
- Used orphan branches and cherry-picks to restructure root commits without losing metadata

### Browser Compatibility
- Ensured HTML5 documents remain readable in older browsers by keeping presentational table layout attributes
- Maintained legacy `<center>`, `<TABLE BORDER=0 CELLSPACING=0 CELLPADDING=0>`, and alignment attributes alongside modern structure
- Avoided removing structural markup that older rendering engines depend on

## Tools Used
- Git (rebase, cherry-pick, filter-branch alternatives via orphan branches)
- PowerShell scripting for bulk text transformations
- Manual regex-based HTML attribute replacement with careful content preservation

## Lesson Learned
When modernising heritage HTML, prioritise **content preservation** and **incremental change**: keep the document structure that browsers rely on, extract only the styling, and let global CSS carry the visual consistency.
